// D9471 control: a record literal holding an un-annotated function whose result the record
// type's function field accepts. The field reads it at `(i32) => f64`, so every cell prints
// `1.5`; the refusal of the wrong-result twin must not reach it.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
type R = { f: (a: i32) => f64 }
function half(a) { return a / 2.0 }
// @@VALUE@@
{ f: half }
// @@TYPE@@
R
// @@PROOF@@
print(v.f(3))
// @@WANT@@
1.5
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a record, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
